  "limits_and_remaining_work": [
    "Metadata policy permits exact changes implied by the resource script. It does not establish universal ctime ABA detection after the application itself moved an original root or changed a directory namespace. ACL/extended-attribute values and filesystem flags are not separately captured, so further property enforcement after own ctime changes remains open. Created objects keep their existing ownership receipts rather than a new complete metadata baseline.",
    "Installed Local fixtures use OPFS correspondence and native discovery folders. Access-loss tests do not establish a physical browser permission prompt; review-bearing physical-folder PWA verification remains separate.",
    "The native implementation executes on macOS and in the recorded Linux arm64 tooling container. The Linux container has a 2 CPU / 4 GiB / no-swap build budget; it is not a complete-app 2 GiB workload measurement. Windows all-target compilation does not establish native Windows behavior.",
    "Independent-provider interleavings, full mutation/child/cross-process ownership and filesystem-event/transitive runtime coverage remain unfinished.",
    "Complete retained/in-flight memory, hard cache/output bounds, reusable-result keys, editor prefetch scheduling and measured benefit, Terraform public SDK/toolkit pins and publication remain unfinished.",
    "This is the affected 13-case matrix, rebuilt installed contracts and four Linux native checks, not the final complete pre-push integration/browser/editor/font/real-server suite. The two existing ignored tests remain unexecuted in both native runs. No commit, push, publication or exact-head hosted CI is implied. Editor performance remains parked."
  ]
